# OS / editor noise
.DS_Store

# Obsidian local state — plugins, layout, hotkeys. Churns constantly and is
# machine-local; Obsidian Sync covers the backup case.
/.obsidian
/.trash

# Staging area for fresh web clippings, before they're cleaned up and
# promoted into inbox/. Not ready to be read, let alone published.
/Clippings

# Ingest queue: articles waiting to be ingested, moved to source/ once done.
# Raw third-party content, same as source/ below.
/inbox

# Raw sources: verbatim copies of other people's articles, kept locally for
# the LLM to read. Not redistributed — every wiki page cites its source URL
# in its `## Sources` section, so the originals stay reachable.
# NOTE: this means source/ is NOT backed up by git. Obsidian Sync (or your
# own backup) is the only copy.
/source
